# Passwordless sudo for vpnCLI — GENERATED, do not edit by hand.
#
# `vpnctl install-sudoers` renders this template with the values detected on
# THIS machine (user, helper, openfortivpn path, config path, pid path) and installs
# the result to the configured sudoers path, suffixed for this backend
# (default /etc/sudoers.d/vpncli-fortivpn — see ACTIVE_SUDOERS_PATH), so it
# never clobbers the openvpn backend's own rule file, validated with
# `visudo -cf`.
#
# Passwordless sudo only applies to the EXACT command lines below. All commands are
# rendered from the same paths the tool actually runs, so:
#   - the helper starts and supervises the VPN process,
#   - status verifies the PID belongs to the expected VPN command, and
#   - stop verifies the expected VPN command before terminating its recorded PID.
# Because it is generated per machine, moving the repo can never desync it again.
#
# Re-run `vpnctl install-sudoers` after changing the openfortivpn path or the
# config location.

__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: __HELPER__ start-fortivpn __EXPECT__ __OPENFORTIVPN__ __CONFIG__ __PID_FILE__
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: __HELPER__ status __OPENFORTIVPN__ __CONFIG__ __PID_FILE__
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: __HELPER__ stop __OPENFORTIVPN__ __CONFIG__ __PID_FILE__
